<title>ISRAEL: Koor says postpones Yankee bond issue.</title>
<headline>Koor says postpones Yankee bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koor Industries Ltd, Israel's largest industrial concern, said on Monday it had decided to postpone a Yankee bond offering planned for July in light of Israel's exchange rate reform.</p>
<p>Koor had planned to issue $200 million to $300 million in Yankee bonds. A company spokesman said Koor was now weighing the possibility of a bond issue in Tel Aviv.</p>
</text>
